The game does not start with several large displays attached (the launcher never appears)

Before the launcher opens, the game lists every display mode each display offers (D3DEnum_DisplayModeCallback 0x40600d,
called by DirectDraw for D3DEnum_DDrawDeviceCallback 0x4062e5) into a table of 100 modes, with no limit. That table is
inside a D3DDeviceInfo on the stack of D3DEnum_DDrawDeviceCallback, so the 101st mode lands on the table's own count and
every later one is written further up the stack, over that frame's pointers and return address and over its callers'.
DirectDraw offers each resolution once per depth (32, 16 and 8 bits), so a display with more than about 33 resolutions
overflows it. A 6K monitor running scaled offers 38; a MacBook's built-in screen offers 22, which is why the game
starts with the laptop alone and not with the monitors attached.

This fix keeps only the depths the game's devices can render (16, 24 and 32 bits: D3DEnum_D3DDeviceCallback drops the
rest anyway) and stops at the table's 100 entries. The launcher lists the same modes as before.

Files: src/app/d3dapp.cpp (D3DEnum_DisplayModeCallback).

diff --git a/src/app/d3dapp.cpp b/src/app/d3dapp.cpp
index 2571366..05a433c 100644
--- a/src/app/d3dapp.cpp
+++ b/src/app/d3dapp.cpp
@@ -805,6 +805,12 @@ HRESULT __stdcall D3DEnum_DisplayModeCallback(DDSURFACEDESC2 *pddsd, void *pCont
 {
     /* cast kept: the enumeration context is the D3DDeviceInfo the caller passed */
     D3DDeviceInfo *pInfo = (D3DDeviceInfo *)pContext;
+    /* FIX display-mode-overflow: the table holds 100 modes and the caller's copy of it is on its stack, so a display
+     * offering more overwrote that frame and its callers'. Only the depths the game's devices render (16, 24, 32 bits)
+     * are kept, and none past the table's end. */
+    DWORD bits = pddsd->ddpfPixelFormat.dwRGBBitCount;
+    if ((bits != 16 && bits != 24 && bits != 32) || pInfo->modeCount >= 100)
+        return DDENUMRET_OK;
     MODES(pInfo)[pInfo->modeCount] = *pddsd;
     pInfo->modeCount++;
     return DDENUMRET_OK;
